# ---- Package data sets ------------------------------------------------------------

#' Simulated PSQI and actigraphy data of the worked example
#'
#' The simulated data set analysed in the manuscript, generated by
#' `simulate_sleep_data(seed = 20261003)`: seven PSQI component scores, the
#' PSQI global score, an actigraphy sleep-quality index and the true latent
#' trait. [sleep_data()] returns it without `eta_true`, and [sleep_eta_true()]
#' returns `id` and `eta_true`.
#'
#' @format A data frame with 1000 rows and 11 columns:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{id}{person identifier, 1 to 1000}
#'   \item{C1}{PSQI component 1, subjective sleep quality (0 to 3)}
#'   \item{C2}{PSQI component 2, sleep latency (0 to 3)}
#'   \item{C3}{PSQI component 3, sleep duration (0 to 3)}
#'   \item{C4}{PSQI component 4, habitual sleep efficiency (0 to 3)}
#'   \item{C5}{PSQI component 5, sleep disturbances (0 to 3)}
#'   \item{C6}{PSQI component 6, use of sleeping medication (0 to 3)}
#'   \item{C7}{PSQI component 7, daytime dysfunction (0 to 3)}
#'   \item{PSQI_global}{PSQI global score, the sum of C1 to C7 (0 to 21)}
#'   \item{SQI}{actigraphy sleep-quality index, higher = better sleep, rounded to 0.1}
#'   \item{eta_true}{true latent sleep-disturbance trait, N(0, 1); for evaluation only}
#' }
#' @source Simulated: `simulate_sleep_data(seed = 20261003)`, GRM items of
#'   [true_items] and SQI = 72 - 8 eta - 1.5 eta^2 + N(0, 6^2).
"psqi_sleep"

#' NHANES 2001-2002 gait speed and mobility items, ages 60+
#'
#' Gait speed from the timed 20-ft walk and seven lower-body mobility items of
#' the physical functioning questionnaire for NHANES 2001-2002 participants
#' aged 60+ with a valid walk time and at least one item answered. Analyses
#' are unweighted. [gait_data()] returns these data, optionally filtered or
#' recoded, together with the item matrix.
#'
#' @format A data frame with 1426 rows and 15 columns:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{SEQN}{NHANES respondent sequence number}
#'   \item{age}{age in years at screening (60 to 85; 85 = 85 or older)}
#'   \item{sex}{1 = male, 2 = female}
#'   \item{walk_time}{time to walk 20 ft, seconds}
#'   \item{gait_speed}{gait speed, m/s (6.096 m / walk_time)}
#'   \item{walking_aid}{1 = walking-aid user (needs special equipment to walk,
#'     used a device in the walk test, or could not walk unassisted), 0 = not}
#'   \item{C1}{difficulty walking a quarter mile (0 = no difficulty, 1 = some,
#'     2 = much, 3 = unable; NA if missing or not asked)}
#'   \item{C2}{difficulty walking up 10 steps (coded as C1)}
#'   \item{C3}{difficulty walking between rooms on the same floor (coded as C1)}
#'   \item{C4}{difficulty standing up from an armless chair (coded as C1)}
#'   \item{C5}{difficulty getting in and out of bed (coded as C1)}
#'   \item{C6}{difficulty stooping, crouching or kneeling (coded as C1)}
#'   \item{C7}{difficulty standing for long periods (coded as C1)}
#'   \item{n_items_answered}{number of items C1 to C7 answered (1 to 7)}
#'   \item{needs_equipment}{1 = needs special equipment to walk (PFQ055 = 1);
#'     C1 and C2 are not asked of these people}
#' }
#' @source NHANES 2001-2002 public-use files MSX_B (lower extremity
#'   functioning), PFQ_B (physical functioning) and DEMO_B (demographics),
#'   National Center for Health Statistics,
#'   <https://wwwn.cdc.gov/nchs/nhanes/>. Built by `inst/scripts/gait_data.R`.
"gait"
